ementation code while builders do not see tests, enhancing test accuracy and separation of concerns.\n- Established a new test folder structure mirroring the packages directory, ensuring organized and accessible test files.\n- Updated documentation to reflect changes in test creation and CI processes, emphasizing the removal of `dist` from the tests repository.","tree":{"sha":"c69edc8730efd9b645efe766f3ca76f649f0248f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Resnovas/Eventiva/git/trees/c69edc8730efd9b645efe766f3ca76f649f0248f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Resnovas/Eventiva/git/commits/1d9dc1aa235e54dda1c3943a93a772af07dec74a","verification":{"payload":"tree c69edc8730efd9b645efe766f3ca76f649f0248f\nparent 63f23346a8fd4c7465e66f61b81c51d06f4400d7\nauthor Jonathan Stevens <jonathan.stevens@resnovas.com> 1773578947 +0000\ncommitter Jonathan Stevens <jonathan.stevens@resnovas.com> 1773578947 +0000\n\nAdd Effect Vitest TDD and Tests Bootstrap Plan\n\n- Introduced a new plan for bootstrapping Effect/Vitest tests directly in the main repository, allowing for inline test authoring and syncing to the Eventiva/tests repository.\n- Redesigned CI workflows to ensure test creators have full access to implementation code while builders do not see tests, enhancing test accuracy and separation of concerns.\n- Established a new test folder structure mirroring the packages directory, ensuring organized and accessible test files.\n- Updated documentation to reflect changes in test creation and CI processes, emphasizing the removal of `dist` from the tests repository.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOw2R1GUopWyn4HFyGzaJLu85cn\nNLOl6UK81riqa0nIoAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKlpNUT0E90xI8xCQtINDXALzUQtn9FphCLOB2EwSLYXDNPglJRpWmyW2X+NdxFX6m\nCP9txk3/HKc0RJr2nkJAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-15T12:49:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https:/